/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ammoniaRate01_dyson_simon -- the ammonia synthesis rate law on the bench.

  THE PACKAGE BELOW IS A FORMALITY AND SAYS SO.  `rateLawBench` evaluates
  the law written in constant/reactions; it never touches the thermophysical
  package,
  because Dyson & Simon carry their OWN fugacity coefficients (Eqs 6-8) and
  their OWN equilibrium constant (Eq 2, after Gillespie & Beattie).  That is
  the point of the case rather than an omission: the rate law is an
  INDEPENDENT source, and comparing it with what Choupo's own SRK + Gibbs
  minimisation says is a comparison between two sources instead of a model
  checking itself.  See README.md section 4 -- they agree to 0.63 %.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
application  choupoProps;
tier         tutorial;
description  "The ammonia synthesis rate of Dyson & Simon (1968), WRITTEN in the case (constant/reactions, `type expression`, every constant with its unit and equation number) and put on the rate-law bench: Eq 19's pseudo-homogeneous rate, Eq 39's effectiveness factor as a declared table over Table I's three pressures, Eq 40, a declared 150-300 atm window and an announced pressure interpolation; the paper's anchors are held by a gate on every case's copy of the law. It locates the LOCUS OF MAXIMUM RATE at three conversions and shows it descending -- the curve ammonia03_quench_converter zigzags about -- and evaluates the rate at that converter's own bed states.";
verbosity    3;
